WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.272 --> 00:00:16.343
"Tom!" yelled Aunt Polly.

2
00:00:17.104 --> 00:00:18.085
There was no answer.

3
00:00:18.105 --> 00:00:20.687
"Tom!" she shouted again.

4
00:00:20.707 --> 00:00:23.149
"Where is that boy?"

5
00:00:23.529 --> 00:00:24.050
she muttered.

6
00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:29.294
Aunt Polly looked everywhere for her young nephew, but he was nowhere to be found.

7
00:00:30.295 --> 00:00:31.376
He wasn't in his bedroom.

8
00:00:32.384 --> 00:00:34.706
He wasn't in the yard, and he wasn't in the kitchen.

9
00:00:36.468 --> 00:00:40.051
Aunt Polly knew that if she couldn't see Tom, he was probably getting into trouble.

10
00:00:41.272 --> 00:00:44.174
Tom was an orphan, and he loved mischief and adventure.

11
00:00:45.335 --> 00:00:47.016
But sometimes he was too mischievous.

12
00:00:47.036 --> 00:00:50.379
"When I find you, I'll give you a spanking."

13
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.020
Aunt Polly shouted.

14
00:00:52.781 --> 00:00:53.922
Then she grabbed the broom.

15
00:00:53.942 --> 00:00:57.845
"Where on earth has that boy gone?"

16
00:00:58.266 --> 00:00:59.427
Aunt Polly said to herself.

17
00:01:01.804 --> 00:01:02.704
"T-o-m-m!" she screamed.

18
00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:06.446
Her glasses fell to the tip of her long, narrow nose.

19
00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:11.088
As she pushed the glasses back up, she spied something moving under the bed.

20
00:01:11.108 --> 00:01:13.729
"I've got you now, boy!"

21
00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.411
Aunt Polly took the broom handle and quickly pushed it under the bed.

22
00:01:19.351 --> 00:01:22.452
She wasn't surprised when she struck something, but it wasn't Tom.

23
00:01:23.313 --> 00:01:26.854
Instead her cat sprang out from under the bed with an angry howl.

24
00:01:28.515 --> 00:01:33.081
Just then Aunt Polly heard footsteps behind her, and she turned to see Tom sneaking out of the

25
00:01:33.121 --> 00:01:38.623
closet. Aunt Polly grabbed the boy by his shirt and gave him a quick shake and a long

26
00:01:38.663 --> 00:01:42.645
look. His hands were filthy, and he was grinning from ear to ear.

27
00:01:42.665 --> 00:01:45.486
"What were you doing in the closet?"

28
00:01:45.966 --> 00:01:46.746
asked Aunt Polly.

29
00:01:46.766 --> 00:01:51.008
"Nothing," said Tom sheepishly.

30
00:01:51.028 --> 00:01:54.129
"Nothing!" shouted Aunt Polly.

31
00:01:54.149 --> 00:01:55.790
"Look at your hands.

32
00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.311
Look at your mouth.

33
00:01:57.751 --> 00:01:59.111
Why are you so filthy?"

34
00:01:59.131 --> 00:02:02.376
"I don't know," said Tom innocently.

35
00:02:02.396 --> 00:02:05.757
"Well, I know," said his aunt.

36
00:02:05.777 --> 00:02:10.779
"It's jam, and I've told you a hundred times to leave that jam alone.

37
00:02:11.599 --> 00:02:13.820
Go back into the closet and get me my stick."

38
00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:17.921
Tom gave Aunt Polly the willow stick reluctantly.

39
00:02:17.941 --> 00:02:21.842
"I'm really in trouble now," thought Tom.

40
00:02:23.062 --> 00:02:27.064
As Aunt Polly raised the stick, Tom shouted, "Look behind you!

41
00:02:27.704 --> 00:02:28.344
What's that?"

42
00:02:29.384 --> 00:02:33.586
Aunt Polly turned to look, and in a flash, Tom ran out the door and jumped over the

43
00:02:33.646 --> 00:02:38.888
fence. "Oh, darn that boy!"

44
00:02:39.388 --> 00:02:42.009
Aunt Polly sighed, and then she began to laugh.

45
00:02:45.551 --> 00:02:46.331
will I learn?

46
00:02:47.011 --> 00:02:49.392
He's played that trick on me a thousand times.

47
00:02:50.252 --> 00:02:53.554
People say 'an old fool is the biggest fool,' and they're right.

48
00:02:54.254 --> 00:02:55.995
I should know all his tricks by now."

49
00:02:57.535 --> 00:02:59.016
Aunt Polly worried about Tom.

50
00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:04.161
She wanted him to become a good man, but he got into too much trouble and skipped a

51
00:03:04.221 --> 00:03:04.881
lot of school.

52
00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:10.483
"If I find out that boy has skipped school again, I'll have to punish him," she said to

53
00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:15.644
herself. "'Spare the rod and spoil the child,' as the Bible says.

54
00:03:16.584 --> 00:03:20.205
I know the Bible is right because that boy is a very sinful creature.

55
00:03:21.086 --> 00:03:23.686
It's all my fault because I don't like to beat him."

56
00:03:24.887 --> 00:03:29.908
While Aunt Polly was blaming herself for Tom's faults, Tom was preparing to celebrate his mischief.

57
00:03:32.388 --> 00:03:34.669
"I deserve a vacation," thought Tom.

58
00:03:34.689 --> 00:03:41.093
"After all, I made Aunt Polly believe that something was actually behind her for the thousandth time.

59
00:03:41.913 --> 00:03:44.935
And they just don't teach you useful tricks like that at school."

60
00:03:45.835 --> 00:03:48.837
So Tom skipped school, and he had a very good time.

61
00:03:51.218 --> 00:03:53.860
Tom got home just in time to help Jim with his chores.

62
00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:57.722
Jim was the young slave who helped Aunt Polly with the housework.

63
00:03:58.782 --> 00:04:01.264
Tom entertained Jim with the tales of his adventures.

64
00:04:02.176 --> 00:04:06.379
Tom's half brother, Sid, listened too because he had already finished his chores.

65
00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.902
Sid was the opposite of Tom in almost every way.

66
00:04:12.383 --> 00:04:16.346
At dinner Aunt Polly wanted to punish Tom for eating the jam and fooling her with his old

67
00:04:16.406 --> 00:04:21.070
trick. So she asked Tom many questions, hoping to catch him in a lie.

68
00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:25.092
"Tom, it was quite warm at school today, wasn't it?"

69
00:04:25.112 --> 00:04:27.074
"Oh yes, ma'am.

70
00:04:27.594 --> 00:04:29.696
It was very warm," answered Tom.

71
00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:33.161
"Didn't you want to swim in the river?"

72
00:04:33.621 --> 00:04:34.442
asked Aunt Polly.

73
00:04:35.382 --> 00:04:38.823
Tom nervously looked at Aunt Polly's face, but it told him nothing.

74
00:04:40.144 --> 00:04:44.166
He said, "I did want to go swimming, but I had to go to school."

75
00:04:45.066 --> 00:04:46.767
Aunt Polly felt Tom's shirt collar.

76
00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:50.268
It was dry, and for a minute she just stared at Tom.

77
00:04:50.288 --> 00:04:57.632
"The dry collar is a trick I've used a million times, but she's never figured it out," thought

78
00:04:57.672 --> 00:05:02.049
Tom. He tried to hide his smile as he watched his aunt's face carefully.

79
00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:06.315
Was Aunt Polly about to punish him, or had he fooled her once again?
